The second argument to tcp4_seq_show can be SEQ_START_TOKEN (value 0x1), which
indicates the header row.
Check for this before treating it as a struct sock pointer.
Save seq->count in the entry handler either way, but skip the port check on the
header.

To convert the port number to a string for matching against port_targets, use
snprintf into a small stack buffer.
Then pass that string to rk_target_match.

The seq_file pointer is the first argument (regs->di).
Cast it and access seq->count directly.
Restoring count to the saved value is all it takes to suppress the line.
